/// Synopsis: the documented limits of the animations, each next to its way out where it has one: a `#pause` between the lines of a `>` box shows the box whole on the first step (its bottom edge lightly veiled) and holds back only what follows it; quotations on consecutive lines show on the first step as plain text in quotation marks, while quotations separated by blank lines are revealed one per step; with this theme, Touying's `#item-by-item` shows every item on every step; a `#speaker-note` glued to the items shows the covered item (the note after a blank line does not); a covered line glued to a visible one and followed by a shape shows on the first step (the `#pause` in a paragraph of its own veils it); a `#pause` in a column leaves the callout and the shape of the next column partly unveiled (`#uncover` around them veils them whole); an `#uncover` around an item right after another item of a list does not veil it (a `#pause` between the items does); in a list right inside an `#align(center)` the marker of the covered item stands in the middle on the first step and goes to the left margin on the next, as in Touying's own themes (the list centered as a block, `#align(center, block(align(left)[..]))`, keeps it in place); a list split by a `#pause` counts from 1 under a `#set enum(start: 3)` (the first number written keeps it). The other limits are tested elsewhere: "Unsupported mark" in `tests/errors/`, the covered content that runs on to the next page in `sections/pause-overflow`.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
